  "notes": "Luddy School of Informatics, Computing, and Engineering B.S. in Informatics (bulletin 2026-2027). Informatics Core = 26 cr (INFO-I 101/201/202/210/211/300/308, INFO-Y 395). Additional Luddy requirements: Diversity in the U.S., English Composition (C or higher), Intensive Writing, Statistics, Ethics, 9 cr Natural & Mathematical Sciences. Plus IU Common Ground gen-ed (A&H 6, S&H 6, World Languages & Cultures 6; MATH-M 118 satisfies Math Modeling). Students complete an Informatics Cognate (15 cr, advisor-guided; e.g., Business, Biology, Cognitive Science) and Informatics electives (9 cr). Capstone via INFO-I 494 (prereq INFO-I 211) or approved capstone sequence. Prerequisite chains from the Luddy handbook flowchart: I101 -> I201/I202; I202 -> I300; I201 -> I210; I210 -> I211/I308; I211 -> I494. Minimum 2.0 GPA; C or higher in major courses.",
